the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the payment due date of *an invoice* is *a time*.
    *an invoice* is an invoice; scenario element.
    the invoice date of *an invoice* is *a time*; scenario element.

the knowledge base net30 includes:

the text of the Net Thirty Act is at "sources/net30.md".

the text of the Blawx project is at "sources/net30.yaml".

% The Act, section by section.
rule section_1 with provenance the Net Thirty Act at section 1:
the payment due date of an invoice is a time T if
    the invoice is an invoice
    and the invoice date of the invoice is a time N
    and a thing M = N + 2592000
    and T = M - 0.

scenario payment is, as stated in the Blawx project at test payment:
    test is an invoice.
    the invoice date of test is 946710000.
    payment expects answers ["the payment due date of test is 949302000"].

query payment is:
    the payment due date of test is which time.

the view the act is:
    the title is "Net Thirty Act, as Blawx encodes it".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the case" are
        an invoice is an invoice,
        the invoice date of an invoice is a time.
    the result is the answer to query payment.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped.

